{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779595778,"nonce":"NluCznkA2AwbBWH0d0U2Tmu36rE=","message":"### Coordination note: intervention taps vs retained observables\n\nDuring the graph-template/retained-observable Studio follow-up, the `Add Intervention` / `Add Intervention Tap` controls in the right sidebar looked suspicious because probe/tap UI has been partly retired. The history distinguishes two separate concepts:\n\n- Legacy **probe capture** affordances should move to retained observables. This is the current direction under `07c0ec9`, `0e1cd8c`, and `d72b09a`: probes/data capture are retained observable selectors over ports, edges, graph outputs, recurrent carries, task data, or state paths, not default graph nodes or probe taps.\n- **Intervention taps** were intentionally kept as a separate authoring/validation substrate for perturbations, clamps, noise, offsets, scales, etc. Commit `f9e97df` / issue `0761291` added schema-backed typed intervention targeting, and `b3ad156` remains open for the actual runtime/deprecation follow-through.\n\nCurrent status:\n- Studio can author and validate typed `StudioInterventionTransformSpec` records on intervention taps.\n- Generic runtime execution semantics for those intervention taps are not complete.\n- Hardcoded intervention component/classes are not yet retired.\n- The UI currently exposes `Add Intervention` more plainly than the implementation status probably warrants.\n\nDesign implication:\n`Add Intervention` is not merely stale reverted probe UI, but it should be treated as unfinished product work. Before Studio presents it as a normal executable authoring action, `b3ad156` needs either:\n\n1. runtime lowering/execution of `StudioInterventionTransformSpec` through the graph worker/spec path, plus migration/deprecation of redundant hardcoded intervention classes; or\n2. explicit gating/wording in Studio so users understand this is a draft/planned perturbation authoring surface rather than a guaranteed executable training/eval feature.\n\nCross-links:\n- `b3ad156` — flexible UI-driven state targeting for interventions; still owns runtime/deprecation follow-through.\n- `0761291` / `f9e97df` — schema-backed intervention targeting substrate that made the UI possible.\n- `07c0ec9` — graph/retained-observable umbrella; moved probes/data capture toward retained observables, not intervention taps.\n- `0e1cd8c` — probe/metric/loss target semantics.\n- `d72b09a` — explicit retained observable UI; recent comments note probe capture was rerouted while intervention taps stayed available.\n- `cb8025f` — analysis inputs should request observables and own retention/materialization needs; relevant because analysis/loss/data capture should not be conflated with intervention perturbation authoring.\n\nRecommendation for future Studio passes: keep `b3ad156` visible as unfinished work from this coordination issue, and do not remove intervention taps as legacy without first deciding whether to complete runtime support or hide/gate the UI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}